gate: OPEN
v:4 role:dev x:frontend
task: S89 T2 — Event settings persist on the server
requires: [FRONTEND_DEV]
sprint: S89

context: |
  Events tab and Notification settings both POST /ws/savevea, then GET
  /ws/getvea. A save the server ignores looks like a snap-back. Notification
  settings revert state and set error with no toast. The POST must keep
  every field GET returned (including ones the UI does not edit) and overlay
  only toggles plus T1 thresholds.

steps:
  1. Build the POST from the last GET object. Overlay UI booleans and the
     T1 numbers. Do not rebuild a partial object that drops server fields.
  2. After POST, GET again. If speedingEvent, speedingValue, or a toggled
     flag differs from what was sent, treat the save as failed.
  3. Events tab already toasts eventSettingsSaveFailed. Notification
     settings must toast the same failure and keep the reverted config.
  4. Do not copy the old Android geofence-to-satellite mapping.
     enterEvent and leaveEvent stay the geofence flags.

out:
  - src/screens/object-details/lib/vehicle-event-config-ui.ts
  - src/screens/object-details/hooks/useObjectDetailsHistory.ts
  - src/store/useNotificationStore.ts
  - src/screens/notification-settings/hooks/useNotificationSettingsScreen.ts

done:
  - A toggle and a speeding value survive leaving the screen and reopening.
  - Failed save shows an error toast on both screens.
  - Fields the UI does not show are unchanged on the server.
